    "question": "Josh had 100 gummy bear candies. He decided to give his 3 siblings 10 candies each. Then he gave half of the remaining candies to his best friend. If he only wants to eat 16 gummy bear candies, how many candies are left to be shared with others?",
    "gold": "19",
    "answer": "Josh gave a total of 3 x 10 = <<3*10=30>>30 candies to his siblings.\nHe was then left with 100 - 30 = <<100-30=70>>70 candies.\nHe gave 70/2 = <<70/2=35>>35 candies to his best friend.\nSo he had 70 - 35 = <<70-35=35>>35 candies left.\nSince he only wants to eat 16 candies, there are still 35 - 16 = <<35-16=19>>19 candies left to be shared with others.\n#### 19"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many gummy bear candies are left to be shared with others, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of candies given to Josh's siblings:**\n   Josh has 3 siblings and he gives each of them 10 candies.\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 10 = 30\n   \\]\n   So, Josh gives away 30 candies to his siblings.\n\n2. **Calculate the remaining candies after giving to his siblings:**\n   Josh originally had 100 candies. After giving 30 candies to his siblings, the remaining number of candies is:\n   \\[\n   100 - 30 = 70\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of candies given to his best friend:**\n   Josh then gives half of the remaining 70 candies to his best friend.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{70}{2} = 35\n   \\]\n   So, Josh gives away 35 candies to his best friend.\n\n4. **Calculate the remaining candies after giving to his best friend:**\n   After giving 35 candies to his best friend, the remaining number of candies is:\n   \\[\n   70 - 35 = 35\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the number of candies Josh wants to eat:**\n   Josh wants to eat 16 candies.\n\n6. **Calculate the number of candies left to be shared with others:**\n   The number of candies left to be shared with others is the remaining candies after giving some to his best friend, which is 35.\n\nTherefore, the number of candies left to be shared with others is \\(\\boxed{35}\\).",
